  "text": "Reading\nQuestions 18-22\nComplete the summary using the list of words, A-H, below.\nWrite the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 18-22 on your answer sheet.\nStudies on digital screen use\nThere have been many studies on digital screen Use, SHOWING SOME 18 ....cscssssssseeseieeieeineee\ntrends. Psychologist Anne Mangen gave high-school students a short story to read, half\nusing digital and half using print mediums. Her team then used a question-and-answer\ntechnique to find OUt NOW 19 ......essssuseeeeee @ACH Group’s understanding of the plot\nwas. The findings showeda clear pattern in the responses, with those who read screens\nfinding the order of information 20osc LO recall.\nStudies by Ziming Liu show that students are tending to read 24 neeeceseesseseeeneeeneeeeene\nwords and phrases in a text to save time. This approach, she says, gives the reader a\nsuperficial understanding Of the 22 0... CONtent Of material, leaving no time\nfor thought.\nA\nfast\nB _\nisolated\nC\nemotional\nD_~\nworrying\nE\nmany\nF\nhard\nG\ncombined\nH\nthorough\nQuestions 23-26\nDo the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 2?\nIn boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet, write\nYES\nif the statement agrees with the views of the writer\nNO\nif the statement contradicts the views of the writer\nNOT GIVEN_\nif itis impossible to say what the writer thinks about this\n23\nThe medium we use to read can affect our choice of reading content.\n24\nSome age groups are more likely to lose their complex reading skills than others.\n25\nFalse information has become more widespread in today’s digital era.\n26\nWe still have opportunities to rectify the problems that technology is presenting.\n>/@ p.128)\n89\nIELTSXpress.com\n",
